F-1 (Foxy portability): build DLIO on Foxy/focal as well as Humble/jammy.

The G1's onboard computer runs ROS 2 Foxy on Ubuntu 20.04. Three differences,
none of which changes the odometry:

1. CMake. rosidl_get_typesupport_target() is Galactic+. Foxy's equivalent is
   rosidl_target_interfaces(), which must be called AFTER the consuming target
   exists — so it sits next to dlio_map_node instead of next to
   rosidl_generate_interfaces(). cpp_typesupport_target simply stays unset on
   Foxy and expands to nothing.

2. Subscription callback. callbackKeyframe() takes `const ConstSharedPtr&`, a
   form Foxy's subscription traits cannot deduce the message type through
   (Galactic+). The subscription now passes a ConstSharedPtr-by-value lambda
   that forwards to it; the callback keeps its signature and its body.

3. PCL smart pointers. pcl::PointCloud<T>::Ptr and pcl::PointIndices::Ptr are
   boost::shared_ptr on PCL 1.10 (focal) and std::shared_ptr from PCL 1.11 on
   (jammy). Upstream's std::make_shared assumed >= 1.11 and does not convert on
   focal. pcl::make_shared exists in both and yields whichever handle ::Ptr
   actually is — same object, same aligned allocator. 21 sites in map.cc and
   odom.cc, including four that constructed a `const` cloud and now construct a
   non-const one and rely on the Ptr -> ConstPtr conversion (identical on both
   handle types).

Applies on top of patch 0006 (which touches only the odom.cc subscriptions).
